# <type>(<scope>): Sentence case summary, under 72 characters
#
# Then a blank line, then the body: why this change exists.
#
# The diff already says what changed. What it cannot say is the problem being solved,
# the constraint that ruled out the obvious approach, or the failure mode that
# odd-looking line prevents. Write that, in prose. Open with the rationale rather than
# restating the summary above.
#
# Reach for a bullet list only when the content is genuinely a list of peers, never as
# a way to enumerate the files you touched.
#
# type: feat fix refactor docs chore test style ci perf build
# scope (optional): lib cli mcp docs ci build ...
#
# feat -> minor bump, fix docs perf -> patch, feat! or a BREAKING CHANGE: footer -> major
# (minor while the version is below 1.0). Everything else bumps nothing.
# Release Please owns every version; never edit one.
#
# Enable this template with:  git config commit.template .gitmessage
# The full conventions are in CONTRIBUTING.md.
